<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian Budget-Main economic projections.</title>
<headline>Australian Budget-Main economic projections.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the main economic forecasts released by Australian Treasurer Peter Costello in his 1997/98 (July/June) budget statement on Tuesday:</p>
<p>		  ACTUAL  ESTIMATE  ----FORECAST-----</p>
<p>		  1995/96 1996/97   1997/98    4 qtrs  1998/99</p>
<p>		  year-av year-av   year-av  to Jun98  year-av</p>
<p>  GDP	    4.1     3.25	3.75	3.75     3.50</p>
<p>  CPI	    4.2     1.25	1.0	 1.75     2.50</p>
<p>Underlying</p>
<p>   inflation   3.2     2.0	 2.0	 2.0	n/a</p>
<p>Unemployment</p>
<p>   rate	  8.5     8.75	8.25	8.0	n/a</p>
<p>  Employment   2.6     1.25	2.0	 2.25     2.25*</p>
<p>Current acc.   deficit     20.1    20.0	21.0	 n/a	n/a</p>
<p>Avg earnings</p>
<p>   growth	4.2     4.75	4.0	 4.0	3.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are percent change on previous year except unemployment, which is the percent rate, and the current account deficit, which is A$ billions. *98/99 employment forecast on national accounts basis, previous years based on labour force survey.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
